window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>The summer solstice has arrived, and, of course, the town of Silverkeep is divided on how to celebrate it. The magical folk, eager to reclaim their traditions after six years in hiding, have requested the town square to hold their event, but it's already been reserved by the transplants, who've grown accustomed to their own ways of celebrating.</p> <p>Assistant Mayor Abora has the bright idea to combine the events, putting both magical and transplant as co-chairs of all the events, which sits well with no one, except Lillie, who has no problem working together with Julian Globe to make desserts. But when magical apothecary Wineke's fireworks go off - and it looks like someone tampered with them - Lillie's on the case to figure out who wants to ruin the celebration before the town rips itself apart.</p> <p>A Dash of Sorcery is the third book in the Pobyd Perfections Bakery Series.</p>"; 
